CREATING requeues as provisioning, UPDATING
requeues as updating, ACTIVE settles success,
and DELETING retains the finalizer until DELETED
or confirmed absence.
Create, update, and delete persist and poll the
OCE work request, recover the OceInstance
identifier, and reread the instance before
projecting status.
Pre-create reuse requires compartmentId,
tenancyId, and name and adopts only one exact
eligible match. Failed or deleting instances are
never reused.
IdcsAccessToken is a create-time secret that OCI
does not echo, so post-create parity normalizes
it away. Only the reviewed update-detail fields
reconcile in place; the remaining identity and
shape fields require replacement, and
ChangeOceInstanceCompartment stays out of scope.
end note
